The '''Revolutionary Front''' ({{lang-bl|Frente Revolucionario}}) is a Baliscan [[W:Platformism|platform]] established to support the confederal abandonment of [[W:Armed neutrality|armed neutrality]] and embrace of [[W:proletarian internationalism|proletarian internationalism]]. It advocates for confederal support for revolutionary parties and movements and [[W:Wars of national liberation|wars of national liberation]] across the world, including through [[W:Cuban military internationalism|military internationalism]]. It rejects the concept of [[W:Peaceful coexistence|peaceful coexistence]], asserting that it has been repeatedly proven that "capitalism anywhere is a threat to socialism everywhere", and supported the [[Mutual Arms and Technology Agreement]]. The Front [[Revolutionary Workers' Front|underwent a schism]] in 1981 due to it's vocal opposition to the [[Kuluba Accords]], which ended the [[Camboriú War|armed conflict]] between Balisca and [[Potocsí]]. 

It argues that peaceful coexistence has been repeatedly proven impossible due to capitalist aggression, and endorses calls for [[W:World revolution|world revolution]]. Additionally, the platform states that instead of waiting for the forces of capitalism to strike first, Balisca (and other [[W:socialist state|socialist states]]) should develop [[W:Nuclear weapons|nuclear weaponry]] and achieve parity with the nuclear capabilities of the capitalist countries in order to defend their revolutionary progress. It supports the establishment of a [[Balisca-Burawa relations|Burawi-Baliscan]] [[W:Nuclear umbrella|nuclear umbrella]]. 

The platform has gained increased popularity as the [[W:Conservative wave|blue tide]] and the surge in [[W:Neo-nationalism|neo-nationalism]] and [[W:Right-wing populism|right-wing populism]] in Abyala (particularly in [[Potocsí]]) continues to intensify confederal debate regarding Balisca's longstanding policy of international neutrality.   

